<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>3.2.4: Self Check</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00721</md:content-id>
    <md:title>3.2.4: Self Check</md:title>
    <md:uuid>51d6363c-78bc-4fe7-8240-2504a14e4c34</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Old Faithful is a geyser in Yellowstone National Park. The following table offers some rough estimates of the length of an eruption (in minutes) and the amount of water (in gallons) in that eruption.</para>
<table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
  <thead/>
  <tbody>
              <row>
                <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">
                  Length (minutes)
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  1.5
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  2
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  3
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  4.5
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">
                  Amount of Water
                      (gallons)
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  3,700
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  4,100
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  6,450
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  8,400
                </entry>
              </row>
            </tbody>
          </table>
<para>Use technology to find an equation of the line of best fit. Round to the nearest hundredth.</para></section>
</content>
</document>
